# MZ-800 1Z-016 BASIC: letters, digits, shifted symbols, cursor keys,
# GRAPH/ALPHA and an F-key.
# BASIC is at Ready by frame 420 with --basic. Each typed character takes
# 8 frames; commands leave ~30 frames after Return so BASIC has finished
# responding before the next key (the MZ-80A has no type-ahead).
420  type "10 PRINT \"Hello 0123456789\""
636  key  Return
666  type "20 PRINT \"!#$%&'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[]^_\""
954  key  Return
# Cursor editing: up two rows onto line 10, right to the H, overtype it.
984  key  Up
992  key  Up
1000 key  Right
1008 key  Right
1016 key  Right
1024 key  Right
1032 key  Right
1040 key  Right
1048 key  Right
1056 key  Right
1064 key  Right
1072 key  Right
1080 type "J"
1088 key  Return
1126 key  Down
# A stored line holding graphic characters typed in GRAPH mode.
1134 type "30 PRINT \""
1214 key  F11             ; GRAPH
1222 type "QWERTY"
1270 key  F12             ; ALPHA
1278 type "\""
1286 key  Return
1316 key  F2              ; default definition: "LIST "
1340 key  Return
1416 type "RUN"
1440 key  Return
